{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed581286445/11/codegen_prompts/3.md\"","aggregated_output":"你要为一个新的 ARC-AGI 风格题目实现代码。代码文件必须包含 `main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray` 和 `generate_input() -> np.ndarray`。\n\n## 新题位置\n\n- 描述目录：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/11`\n- 题号：`3`\n- 目标代码路径：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed581286445/11/3.py`\n\n## 新题描述\n\n<new_puzzle index=\"3\">\n- `description`：利用网格边缘的\"指令条\"编码行列操作序列，对内部图案依次执行镜像翻转和颜色替换操作。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为 black。\n  - 网格的最外一圈是\"指令框\"：顶边和底边各有一行像素，左边和右边各有一列像素，其余位置为 black。\n  - 顶边的像素序列从左到右编码列操作：red 表示\"该列做上下翻转\"，black 表示\"该列不操作\"。\n  - 左边的像素序列从上到下编码行操作：blue 表示\"该行做左右翻转\"，black 表示\"该行不操作\"。\n  - 右边像素序列从上到下编码颜色替换：每个非 black 像素指定该行内所有 green 像素替换为该像素的颜色。\n  - 底边像素序列从左到右编码颜色替换：每个非 black 像素指定该列内所有 yellow 像素替换为该像素的颜色。\n  - 内部区域（去掉最外一圈后）是一个由 green、yellow 和 black 构成的图案。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 第一步：读取顶边指令，对每个标记为 red 的列，将内部区域中该列的像素序列上下翻转。\n  - 第二步：读取左边指令，对每个标记为 blue 的行，将内部区域中该行的像素序列左右翻转。\n  - 第三步：读取右边指令，对指定行执行 green → 对应颜色 的替换。\n  - 第四步：读取底边指令，对指定列执行 yellow → 对应颜色 的替换。\n  - 输出为仅包含内部区域的网格（去掉指令框），尺寸缩小。\n\n- `Key insight`：四条边各自编码不同类型的操作（空间变换 vs 颜色替换），解题者必须分别破译每条边的含义，并发现操作的先后顺序（先翻转再换色）影响最终结果——仅从一个样例无法区分顺序，需要多个样例交叉验证。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n## 机制相似参考题\n\n下面参考题由本地相似度流程自动选择：先用 `annotations`/docstring/代码特征抽取机制标签，再按机制相似度、文本相似度和代码特征相似度重排，并用 MMR 做去重。优先学习这些题的对象识别方式、随机生成器约束、边界条件处理，不要照搬旧题规则。\n\n已选参考：eval/88e364bc, train/412b6263, train/58c02a16, eval/581f7754, eval/dbff022c, train/bae5c565, eval/2d0172a1, train/458e3a53\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"1\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"88e364bc\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3969\nmechanism=0.4514\nlexical=0.0214\ncode_feature=0.7143\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, code:output_resize, code:rotation, object:closed_region, object:frame, object:grid_edge, object:marker, operation:sort_order, relation:direction, relation:inside, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/88e364bc.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/88e364bc.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nSlide yellow pixels inside walled regions in the direction dictated by border-legend arrows.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color; yellow pixels sit inside enclosed regions bounded by colored walls.\n- Border legends: small rectangles on the grid edge whose fill color C matches a region's border color. Each legend contains a center dot and an indicator dot encoding a direction.\n\nRule:\n- For each enclosed region, identify its border color C and look up the legend with fill color C.\n- The direction from the legend's center dot to its indicator dot gives the slide direction.\n- All yellow pixels in that region slide in that direction, stacking against the far wall.\n\nKey insight: Legend fill color links to region border color; the center→indicator offset encodes the movement vector.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"summary\": \"Yellow pixels inside colored-border regions move in the direction indicated by the red pixel in the legend with matching background color, stopping at region boundary.\",\n  \"type\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src\": \"yellow pixels inside colored-border regions s\",\n  \"dst\": null,\n  \"match_cond\": \"\",\n  \"path\": \"move(s, direction=legend.red_pixel_offset) where legend.background_color == s.containing_region.border_color until s.touches(region_boundary)\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"\",\n  \"transform\": \"\",\n  \"symbol_instructions\": \"legend on grid edge with background color C and red pixel indicates: yellow pixels in regions with border color C move in direction from blue center to red pixel\",\n  \"multi_step\": \"\",\n  \"concepts\": [\n    \"legend/control-pixels\",\n    \"region-membership\",\n    \"directional-movement\",\n    \"boundary-collision\"\n  ],\n  \"notes\": \"\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"2\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"412b6263\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3561\nmechanism=0.4307\nlexical=0.0162\ncode_feature=0.5000\noverlap_tags=code:connected_components, code:output_resize, code:rotation, object:closed_region, object:frame, object:marker, operation:crop_resize, operation:reflect, operation:sort_order, relation:inside, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/412b6263.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/412b6263.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nInfer the background, rotate the whole input 90 degrees counterclockwise, and stack two framed copies vertically.\n\nInput structure:\n- Blue is absent from the input.\n- One rare marker color appears in exactly two pixels.\n- The background is the unique non-marker color whose removal leaves exactly two 4-connected foreground objects, each with one marker pixel and one body color.\n- The whole grid, including background and foreground objects, is the sprite to transform.\n\nRule:\n- Rotate the entire input grid 90 degrees counterclockwise.\n- Create a blue one-pixel frame around two vertical copies of the rotated grid.\n- Use the input background color for the two endpoints of every horizontal frame/separator row.\n\nKey insight: The output is not a crop of the foreground objects; it is two copies of the complete rotated input, separated and enclosed by a newly added blue border.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"symmetry/pattern\",\n  \"src\": \"the complete input grid with two marked foreground objects on an inferred background\",\n  \"dst\": \"two vertical slots inside a new one-pixel blue frame\",\n  \"transform\": \"rotate the whole input grid 90 degrees counterclockwise, copy it into both slots, and color each horizontal frame-row endpoint with the inferred background color\",\n  \"grid_shape\": \"rotated input width plus side borders by two rotated input heights plus three frame/separator rows\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"3\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"58c02a16\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3529\nmechanism=0.4560\nlexical=0.0141\ncode_feature=0.3333\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:output_resize, object:frame, object:marker, operation:crop_resize, operation:reflect, operation:sort_order, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/58c02a16.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/58c02a16.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nExpand the top-left seed mask into a recursive colored pattern and tile it across the full grid.\n\nInput structure\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- All foreground lies in a top-left rectangle whose last row and last column are a solid secondary color.\n- Removing that secondary-color row and column leaves a seed region containing background plus one primary color.\n\nRule\n- Use the primary-color pixels in the seed as a binary mask.\n- Replace each primary seed cell with a copy of the seed mask in the primary color, and each background seed cell\n  with a copy of the seed mask in the secondary color.\n- Repeat and crop that expanded tile to the original grid shape.\n\nKey insight\nThe solid L-shaped secondary-color border is a legend, not output content; it supplies the color used when the\nseed's background cells are expanded.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"symmetry/pattern\",\n  \"src\": \"top-left seed region containing background and one primary color, with a solid secondary-color L-shaped legend border\",\n  \"transform\": \"expand the seed mask once: primary seed cells become primary-color copies of the mask, background seed cells become secondary-color copies, and mask background stays background; tile/crop the expanded pattern to the full grid\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"4\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"581f7754\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3536\nmechanism=0.4150\nlexical=0.0143\ncode_feature=0.5714\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, code:output_resize, object:frame, object:grid_edge, object:marker, operation:sort_order, relation:direction, relation:inside, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/581f7754.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/581f7754.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nSlide multi-color sprites to align their marker pixels with matching isolated border anchors.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color.\n- Multi-color sprites in the interior; each has a minority-color \"marker\" pixel.\n- Isolated border pixels (non-bg with all 4-neighbors bg) act as anchors.\n\nRule:\n- Match each sprite to the border anchor sharing its marker color.\n- Top/bottom-edge anchor (non-corner): slide sprite horizontally so marker column = anchor column.\n- Left/right-edge anchor (or corner): slide sprite vertically so marker row = anchor row.\n\nKey insight: The anchor's edge position determines the slide axis — top/bottom means horizontal, left/right (or corner) means vertical.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_to_match\",\n  \"src\": \"multi-color sprite s with a unique marker color (minority color inside s)\",\n  \"dst\": \"align to isolated border pixel d (same marker color)\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"s.marker.color == d.color\",\n  \"transform\": \"translate s: if d on top/bottom edge → align col(s.marker) to col(d); else → align row(s.marker) to row(d); clip out-of-bounds pixels\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"5\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"dbff022c\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3409\nmechanism=0.3799\nlexical=0.0130\ncode_feature=0.6667\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, code:output_resize, object:closed_region, object:frame, object:grid_edge, operation:sort_order, relation:direction, relation:inside, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/dbff022c.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/dbff022c.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nFill hollow sprites' interiors using a color-palette legend on the grid edge.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color. Several hollow sprites with distinct border colors.\n- A small 2×N or N×2 palette block sits on one grid edge; one row/column lists border colors, the other lists corresponding fill colors.\n\nRule:\n- Locate the palette legend on a grid edge and read it as a border→fill color mapping.\n- Find enclosed bg regions (holes) inside sprites that don't touch the grid boundary.\n- For each hole, identify the most common adjacent border color, look it up in the palette, and fill the hole with the mapped fill color.\n\nKey insight: The palette's edge position and orientation determine reading direction; border colors in the palette uniquely key into fill colors.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"summary\": \"Use a color palette legend on the grid edge to fill sprites' interiors based on their border color mapping.\",\n  \"type\": \"transform_in_place\",\n  \"src\": \"hollow sprites with colored borders s\",\n  \"dst\": \"interior of same sprite d\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"d.fill_color == palette_lookup(s.border_color)\",\n  \"path\": \"\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"\",\n  \"transform\": \"fill d with palette[s.border_color]\",\n  \"symbol_instructions\": \"palette is 2xN or Nx2 block on grid edge; read direction based on edge position: top edge reads top-to-bottom, bottom edge reads bottom-to-top, left edge reads left-to-right; first row/column is border color, second is fill color\",\n  \"multi_step\": \"Step 1: locate 2xN or Nx2 palette legend on grid edge; Step 2: build color mapping (border -> fill) based on reading direction; Step 3: for each hollow sprite, lookup border color in palette and fill interior with corresponding fill color\",\n  \"concepts\": [\n    \"color-mapping\",\n    \"lookup-table\",\n    \"flood-fill\",\n    \"border-detection\"\n  ],\n  \"notes\": \"The challenge is correctly reading the palette legend based on its edge position and orientation\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"6\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"bae5c565\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3021\nmechanism=0.3812\nlexical=0.0141\ncode_feature=0.3333\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:output_resize, object:grid_edge, object:marker, operation:reflect, relation:direction, relation:inside, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
